{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-opus-5-5", "id": "msg_011Cge5UGPALJUaC7w2mDhC2", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "I filed two claims, and both beat the record of 1.1566 by more than 0.011 bpb on dev, well past the 0.002 margin. Neither has the full 8 seeds behind it, because I ran out of time. The dev means below come only from fresh seeds that played no part in choosing the variants.\n\n| Claim | Table update schedule (by table, smallest first, in batches) | Claimed dev bpb | Fresh seeds | Seed SD | Gain over record |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | `1,1,1,4,8,8,16,16,16` | 1.1451 | 3 | 0.0003 | 0.0115 |\n| 2 | `1,1,1,8,16,16,32,32,32` | 1.1447 | 4 | 0.0015 | 0.0119 |\n\n**The entry:** it's the record's hashed context mixer with two changes that free up ticks for more training bytes:\n- **Smaller softmax:** bytes are folded by `b % 130` into a 130-way softmax. That about halves the cost of the head and cross entropy. Rare bytes get a small fixed probability at scoring.\n- **Lazy big tables:** the smallest tables update every batch and the largest much less often, because a dense table update costs the same however few rows it touches.\n\n**What the single-seed tests showed (seed 101):**\n- **Helped:** the softmax change with faster small-table updates gave 1.1471. Slowing the big tables further gave 1.1451, 1.1433 and 1.1430.\n- **Did worse:** word contexts (1.1623), thinner high-order rows (1.1497), wider low-order rows (1.1515) and faster mid-table updates (1.1493).\n- **No gain:** a higher table learning rate, a hidden size of 96, batch 128, and four changes to the local-stage constants.\n- **Failed outright:** the hybrid of count tables and mixer scored 3.88 to 4.09. My best guess is hash false hits, because nothing gated the count tables, but I didn't confirm that or retry it.\n\n**Caveats:**\n- **Too few seeds:** the restart below cost about 8 minutes, so I spent the last rounds comparing schedules rather than finishing 8 seeds. The 0.0003 SD on claim 1 comes from only 3 seeds and is probably too low, as claim 2's 0.0015 suggests.\n- **Claims not separated:** the 0.0004 gap between them is within noise, so claim 2 is not shown to be better. It is a correlated second bet, and its claim text says so.\n- **Selection seed:** I chose among about a dozen variants on seed 101, which reads 0.001 to 0.002 lower than fresh seeds. I left it out of the claimed means, so the claimed numbers aren't inflated by that selection.\n- **Causes not isolated:** I never tested the softmax change on its own, so I can't say how much of the gain comes from each change.\n- **Record not rerun:** my baseline run was killed when the sandbox ended the command that launched it, and I chose not to repeat it. The comparison uses your published 1.1566, and the sealed split may shift both numbers.\n- **Final files:** after scoring, I edited the docstring in each `train.py` to describe the final entry. Only smoke runs followed that edit, which passed the static rules and ran end to end. The code below the docstring is unchanged, and the disabled word-context code is still in the files.\n\nThe claims are in `claims/1/` and `claims/2/`, and the experiment files and logs are in `exp/`."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 1645, "cache_read_input_tokens": 129258, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 1645}, "output_tokens": 3, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "61298ef4-bd1a-4ea1-ab67-beb042061337", "uuid": "e1625262-1dd2-4dae-a578-b55428235c56", "timestamp": "2026-11-02T12:10:45.074Z", "request_id": "req_011Cge5UG5oinEM4rJQ2oiuz"}
